          "question": "What is the governing principle of computer science?",
          "answer": "• Core Principle: The study of computer science is guided by the principles of problem-solving, critical thinking, and creativity.\n• Governing Rule: The rules of computer science are based on the laws of mathematics and physics.\n• Application: These principles and rules are applied to design, develop, and test computer systems and programs."
        },
