      "summary": "The excerpt introduces Computer Science as a field fundamentally concerned with the study of computing phenomena, underpinned by mathematical and engineering principles, with a central focus on algorithms as precise instructional sequences enabling computation. It contextualizes CS within a historical continuum of computational devices, from ancient mechanical aids to contemporary digital systems, while simultaneously foregrounding the critical imperative for ethical considerations in its application and societal impact.",
