          "question": "Why is ethical consideration paramount in the application of computer science, and what are its boundary conditions?",
          "answer": "• Computer science outputs profoundly impact societal structures, individual privacy, and global equity, necessitating rigorous caution to ensure ethical deployment and prevent adverse consequences.\n• Ethical boundary conditions involve proactive considerations of data privacy, algorithmic bias, security vulnerabilities, equitable access, and the potential for misuse of powerful computational tools, requiring a continuous assessment of societal impact throughout the development lifecycle."
